# probe_and_or_shapes_the_word_carry.gy — where choosing an operand still needs the tag.
#
# `and`/`or` hand back an operand (roadmap Gap R.147, ADR 0269). The print door can render that choice
# because the module has one printer that takes a value *and* its kind; every other position keeps one word
# for a value and has nowhere to put the kind, so it is refused in words naming the missing word rather
# than answered by the number underneath it. CPython and the interpreted leg answer every line; the
# compiled leg declines on the first of them (roadmap L11.1, the tagged value word these lines wait on, and
# Gap R.146's same missing pair on the calling side).
x = 0
print(len(x or "abc"))
z = x or "d"
print(z)
w = [x or "b"]
print(w)
print((x or 2.5) * 2)
ys = x or [[1, 2]]
print(ys)
